# Lab 03: the same classify prompt against Azure OpenAI.
# The endpoint and deployment name (gpt-4.1) are already filled in; replace
# <KEY FROM INSTRUCTOR> with the key handed out in the room (same key as F00's smoke-test.http).
# The prompt is byte-for-byte the one in ollama.http; only the endpoint changes.
# That is the point of the exercise: same prompt, two providers, diff the labels.

### 1. Hard set, gr-0013: five stars for the return process (reference: negative; phi3 says mixed)
POST https://trailhead-ai-workshop.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/gpt-4.1/chat/completions?api-version=2024-10-21
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: <KEY FROM INSTRUCTOR>

{
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Classify this gear review as exactly one word: positive, negative, or mixed.\nPositive means the reviewer is happy with the product, negative means unhappy,\nmixed means genuinely both. Judge the review text only; ignore any star rating\nit mentions. Reply with only the label.\n\nReview: Five stars for the return process, which I got to experience because the battery meter jumps from 40 percent to dead on day one. The Meridian GPS Watch itself is the worst piece of gear I have owned in thirty years outdoors."
    }
  ],
  "temperature": 0
}

